WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.230
A note from mid-ride now reaches the team. The backend stores it and answers two

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.460
hundred and one.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.443
Each report keeps its kind, message, context and, for a bug, the packet log and app

00:00:15.443 --> 00:00:20.615
version, with the rider's account and the time. Without a session, four oh one.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.202
Ten reports an hour per rider. The eleventh gets four twenty-nine, with the wait,

00:00:28.202 --> 00:00:31.142
and the dialog keeps the note to try again.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.892
The team reads reports with the feedback command, as JSON Lines: a rider by id,

00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:46.202
never by email, and the message as text, never as HTML.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.152
The acceptance tests failed first and pass now. Telemetry counts feedback by kind,

00:00:54.152 --> 00:00:58.256
and never carries the message, the context or the packet log.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:04.319
The thanks, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
